  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the number of ways to choose three points on the geoboard such that triangle $ABC$ is a right triangle with a side length of 2 units and a hypotenuse that is not parallel to any side of the geoboard. The geoboard is a 6x6 grid, and we need to consider the possible right triangles that can be formed with the given constraints.\n\nFirst, let's identify the possible right triangle configurations on a 6x6 geoboard. We can have right triangles with sides that are parallel to the grid lines (e.g., 1x1 and 1x2 unit triangles) or right triangles with hypotenuses that are not parallel to the grid lines.\n\nSince the side length is 2 units, the legs of the right triangle can be either 2 units horizontally and 2 units vertically (forming an L-shape) or 2 units horizontally, 2 units vertically, and a hypotenuse that is not parallel to the grid lines.\n\nHowever, since the hypotenuse must be 2 units, we only need to consider the L-shape configuration with legs of 2 units.\n\nNext, let's count the number of ways to choose three points on the geoboard to form a right triangle with a side length of 2 units. We can choose two points on either the horizontal or vertical direction, and the third point can be chosen such that it forms a right triangle with the two chosen points.\n\nFor the horizontal (or vertical) direction, we can choose two points in 6-1=5 ways (since we cannot choose the same point twice 2.\nJSImport(\"express\");\nimport path from \"path\";\nimport fs from 'fs';\nasync function run(): Promise<void> {\n const app = express();\n \n app.set('port', process.env.PORT || 3010);\n app.set('resolveStatCache', true);\n\n//(app.root = process.cwd()).string;\n(app.static = (path.join(app.root, 'public')));\n\n(async () => {\n    try {\n        await init();\nawait(app.listen(app))\napp.close();\n        } catch (e) {\n            console.log(\"error\", e);\n        }\napp.close();\nconst server = app.listen(app, app.set('port'